Explanation: At the critical point and for a long wire, the conductance moments are proportional to \(\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\mathrm{sech}^{2n}x\,dx\). Thus,
\[
\frac{\langle g^4\rangle}{\langle g\rangle}
=\frac{\int \mathrm{sech}^{8}x\,dx}{\int \mathrm{sech}^{2}x\,dx}
=\frac{32/35}{2}
=\frac{16}{35}.
\]

Answer: \(\boxed{\frac{16}{35}\approx 0.457}\)

