sol_answer:
Explanation: Varying \(\sqrt{-g}Q\) with respect to \(g^{\mu\nu}\), integrating the derivative terms by parts, and using \(\delta \mathcal S_m=-\tfrac12\int\sqrt{-g}\,T_{\mu\nu}\delta g^{\mu\nu}d^4x\) gives
\[
-\frac{2}{\sqrt{-g}}\partial_\alpha(\sqrt{-g}P^\alpha_{\mu\nu})
-P_{\mu\alpha\beta}Q_\nu^{\alpha\beta}
+2Q_\mu^{\alpha\beta}P_{\alpha\beta\nu}
-\frac12Qg_{\mu\nu}
=\frac{8\pi G}{c^4}T_{\mu\nu}.
\]
Expanding the divergence using
\[
\frac{2}{\sqrt{-g}}\partial_\alpha\sqrt{-g}
=g^{\rho\sigma}\partial_\alpha g_{\rho\sigma}
\]
produces the equation in choice A.

Answer: A

Confidence: 97%

